msgid "Devicetree and Open Firmware Subsystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:8
msgid "Other Process Documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:10
msgid ""
"Please see the documents in Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ for "
"information on how to write proper Devicetree bindings and how to submit "
"patches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:14
msgid "Patch Review and Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:16
msgid ""
"Patches handled by Devicetree maintainers are processed differently "
"depending on the patch type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:19
msgid ""
"Core OF driver code, e.g. drivers/of/: patches are reviewed and applied by "
"DT maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:22
msgid ""
"Devicetree bindings: patches are reviewed by DT maintainers, but should be "
"applied by subsystem maintainers except in certain cases.  See also *For "
"kernel maintainers* in Documentation/devicetree/bindings/submitting-patches."
"rst."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:27
msgid ""
"DTS and drivers: DT maintainers might provide comments, but review is "
"generally not expected. DTS must pass schema checks (dtbs_check) or at least "
"do not add any new warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:33
msgid "Patchwork"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:35
msgid ""
"Devicetree maintainers review patches using Patchwork, so the current status "
"of a patch can be checked there. For typical driver submissions, Patchwork "
"receives the entire patch set, but only a few patches are usually Devicetree "
"bindings that are reviewed by DT maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:40
msgid "Explanation of Patchwork statuses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:42
msgid "**New**: Not yet processed by the automation toolset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:43
msgid "**Needs ACK**: Waiting for review by DT maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:44
msgid "**Handled Elsewhere**: Non-DT patch; not being reviewed here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:45
msgid "**RFC**: Patch was likely ignored because it was an incomplete RFC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:46
msgid ""
"**Changes Requested**: Patch was reviewed and DT maintainers expect changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:47
msgid ""
"**Accepted**: Patch was reviewed and applied by DT maintainers to their tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:48
msgid ""
"**Not Applicable**: Patch was reviewed and is likely in good shape, with a "
"*Reviewed-by* or *Acked-by* tag provided, but DT maintainers expect someone "
"else to apply it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:53
msgid "Patch Re-review and Pinging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:55
msgid ""
"Due to the high volume of email traffic, Devicetree maintainers do not read "
"every email they receive and instead rely on Patchwork during the review "
"process. They also often skip patches that have already been reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:59
msgid "As a result, maintainers might miss:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:61
msgid "Questions about already reviewed patches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:62
msgid ""
"Pings, for example when a patch has been reviewed by DT maintainers but has "
"not been picked up by subsystem maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:65
msgid "Such cases can be addressed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:67
msgid "Pinging DT maintainers on the IRC channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/maintainer-devicetree.rst:68
msgid ""
"Dropping the DT maintainer’s *Acked-by* or *Reviewed-by* tag when sending a "
"new version of the patch set, together with an explanation in the patch "
"changelog describing why the tag was removed and what is expected from DT "
"maintainers."
msgstr ""
